title A number and a path naming two different rows
prompt Autonomous lap under the fleet baton -- take the next agent-doable work Lindy-first, crux-first, in the amphora lane.
think Council rota row 3 of 5 (lap 4073, 4073 mod 5 = 3): Water, the row that tastes -- the threshold page, the shape you grew and the shape you are, the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. The seat that landed on this lap is the dual one: diverge by strengthening rather than rewriting, which is what a new reading beside an existing guard is.
think The cold roster pass ran first and answered four reds. One was sow_allow_reach, %493, booked OPEN and another lane's. One was standing_equipment, which reads recorded receipts and so inherits that red. The other two were mine: readme_reach named a broken living link in construction/ITINERARY.md, and reds_fold reds because it runs the reach scan.
think The broken link was the third firing of a shape my own last lap had booked as %495. That lap swept `rows-492.md` to `rows-494.md` through the card with a replace anchored to a bare number, hit a peer's line first, and repaired it by anchoring each replace to its own sentence. The repair moved my block's NUMBER to %494 and left its PATH reading rows-492, one line down, across the card's hard wrap. A sentence-anchored replace cannot see both halves when the wrap falls between them.
think So I asked how wide the class is, and the answer changed the lap. I wrote a throwaway reading over 1,001 living tracked markdown files that finds every link to a REDS fold shelf and compares the numbers in its path against the %N beside it. My first rule -- the nearest preceding %N within one line -- called 32 sentences wrong, and reading them showed every one was honest prose: %220's own shelf citing %218's, a fold recital naming a row's lesson beside a different row's number. A window is not a claim.
think Narrowing to the two shapes that are PROMISES rather than mentions gave a clean field: the anchor text that IS the number (7 sites), and a shelf word whose sentence just named a row (14 sites, all correct). Of the 7 numbered sites, 2 disagreed -- and both were in the shelf file I wrote last lap, published: [%360] pointing at the rows-439-441 shelf for a row that lives on the pin, and [%484] pointing at %480's shelf when %484 has a shelf of its own.
think Four firings of one shape in one day, all from this seat. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, so the lap became the loom rather than a fourth repair.
obs EXISTENCE AND AGREEMENT ARE TWO QUESTIONS, AND ONLY ONE HAD AN INSTRUMENT. readme_reach reads whether a living link OPENS and named exactly one of the four -- the one whose file was absent. The other three all resolve. They open a real shelf holding somebody else's row, which is a misdirection with no expiry: green to every guard the tree has, forever, and a reader following it simply arrives somewhere the sentence never meant. tracked_link asks existence the same way; reds_row_present asks whether the ledger HOLDS a row and never asks who cites it.
obs THE FALSE POSITIVE IS WHY THE FORM IS NARROW, and the narrowing is proven rather than asserted. Two pen cases exist only to hold it: a %N AFTER the link is never its claim (the fold recital's shape, `*Row 170 folded to [link] -- REDS %83's own guard*`), and a %N two lines above is outside the window. Both must be WELCOMED, asserted as hard as any refusal, or the guard would red on 32 honest sentences the day it landed.
obs IT WAS REPLAYED AGAINST THE COMMIT THAT PUBLISHED THE DEFECT, which is the strongest evidence available and cost one worktree. Run against b441f97b2 -- this tree exactly as it stood on the anointed spine -- the scan reads numbered_disagree=3 and names all three sites, including the peer line %495 already recorded. A guard proven only on a repaired tree cannot be told from one that reads nothing.
obs THE PEN CAUGHT A DEFECT IN MY OWN SCAN BEFORE IT SHIPPED, and it was a counting defect, which is this seat's third such in two days. `grep -c ''` prints 0 AND exits 1 on an empty file, so the `|| echo 0` beside it produced a two-line value, `[ "$x" -eq 0 ]` errored out, the emptiness branch was skipped entirely, and a correctly-empty corpus read refused_no_citation rather than refused_no_corpus. awk 'END { print NR }' returns one value and cannot do that. The case that found it was the one asserting the right refusal for the right reason.
obs ONE LINE OF LOOKBACK IS THE BOUND AND IT IS DERIVED, not chosen. The break that shipped fell exactly across the card's hard wrap -- number on one line, link on the next -- so zero lookback would have missed the case that caused the round. Two lines would have reached into the previous paragraph, which is where the false positives live. The pen proves both edges.
obs THE PIN HAD NINE BYTES AGAIN, the second lap running. construction/REDS.md stood at 40,951 of 40,960, so the row could be written only by folding it straight out to its own shelf in the same breath. The card had 20 bytes and took six trims to hold one paragraph, and what came out was my own prior lap's account rather than any peer's -- which is the only reason this round did not have to choose between a peer's paragraph and its own detail. A third ship writing today would have no such luck.
obs WHAT I DID NOT TAKE, AND WHY. %493 is still OPEN and still not mine: sow_allow_reach refuses on any tree with no seed/ projection, no lap makes one, and the fix wants a new capability word in the runner's own probe table plus a control proving it both ways -- an instrument change in another lane, beside custody gate %1. Its cost lands here as standing_equipment reading roster_broken for the second lap, which is honest rather than green.
obs AND THE LANE'S OWN BOOKED LAP IS UNTAKEN. The source's port rendezvous -- reading %485's *the lock stands* -- was this lap's plan until the cold open answered with a live red of my own. Reds first is not a preference here: the broken card link reddened every ship's cold pass, not just mine. The rendezvous design is worked out and written down in the recommend line rather than lost.
loom witness=reds_citation wall_s=3 field_files=26 numbered_links=6 shelf_links=14 pen_cases=23 pen_repos=12
loom scan=reds_citation_first_rule living_md=1001 false_positives=32 note=nearest-preceding-%N, rejected
loom replay=b441f97b2 numbered_disagree=3 note=the tree as published, read in a throwaway worktree
loom pass=standing_equipment_cold guards_run=147 green=139 red=4 gated=4 wall_s=935 tree_moved=no
